{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Phase 2 complete — fix landed for review (Gerrit change 2219)\n\n**Problem** — Closing S3 T3 (67d4-ecba) faulted: a runaway/exhaustion-truncated\ncompletion-verifier run reported a BLOCKING FAIL (exit 1, \"3 unmet criteria\")\nthat only `--force` could bypass, instead of the non-blocking, re-runnable\nINDETERMINATE fault the contract (bug 2a6f) requires.\n\n**Proven root cause** — Two compounding seams downstream of a correctly-firing\nrunaway guard (the guard is NOT the defect):\n- **Seam A (mint)** — `completion_verdict_assembly._restamp_marker` stamped the\n  insufficiency marker only when the criterion's bank entry carried it. A\n  truncated criterion is never banked (`entry is None`), so `_entry_insufficient(None)`\n  is False → the echo branch POPPED the marker → bare `met=false` indistinguishable\n  from a genuine refutation. The omitted-criterion branch of the same function\n  already marked un-banked criteria insufficient; the echo branch was inconsistent.\n- **Seam B (disposition)** — `reconcile_verdict` already derives top-level\n  `evidence_sufficient=False` on an insufficiency-only FAIL, but the close gate and\n  standalone verb only took the retryable exit-11 path when `verdict_obtainable is\n  False`. Insufficiency-only still hard-blocked exit 1.\n\n**Proof** — Held-out RED oracle (5 tests in\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_insufficient_evidence_marker.py`) proven RED first, then\nGREEN (45 passed). Mutation checks: revert Fix A → unbanked-echo tests RED; collapse\nthe disposition helper to always-1 → both retryable-disposition tests RED; restore →\nGREEN. Genuine-unmet FAIL stays a hard block (guard test). Broader related suites\npass with no regressions; `make lint` (complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0) +\n`make typecheck` clean.\n\n**Defect origin** — commit `6b318ffaec4a`, ticket **1d71-a76c-04f6-4642** (\"Mark\nexhausted evidence search as insufficient\"). Its own message reveals both gaps\n(\"stamps... from the bank\"; \"close_precheck still refuses fail-closed\"). Class =\n**plan_defect**. `--caused-by=1d71-a76c-04f6-4642 --class=plan_defect` will be passed\non close.\n\n**Fix** —\n- Fix A: `_restamp_marker` condition → `if record.get(\"met\") is False and (entry is\n  None or _entry_insufficient(entry)):` — un-banked met=false echo stamped\n  insufficient; present markerless entry (genuine refutation) stays bare.\n- Fix B: new pure helper `completion_reconcile.completion_fail_returncode(result)`\n  (returns 11 if `verdict_obtainable is False` OR `evidence_sufficient is False`,\n  else 1); re-exported from `completion.py`; `close_precheck.py` generic raise and\n  `_llm_commands.py` verify-completion verb both route through it; schema description\n  updated. Does NOT overload `verdict_obtainable`; `reconcile_verdict` unchanged.\n\n**Scope & safety** — Caller-dependency sweep: both behavioral consumers already map\n`verdict_obtainable is False`→exit 11; no consumer relies on insufficiency-FAIL=exit\n1. Fix restores (not creates) behaviour, adds no dependency, weakens no test. exit 11\nis retryable and never closes a ticket, so making insufficiency retryable cannot let\nincomplete work close.\n\n**Siblings** — Step 7 Axis 1 (construct): single site, no siblings. Axis 2 (parity):\nall disposition surfaces route through the shared helper or shared close_precheck\ncore; MCP surfaces the raw verdict — NO miss.\n\n**Residual risk** — the runaway `read_file` loop that triggered the truncation is a\nseparate hardening opportunity, filed as bug **3dde-fd6f-8aa3-4c49**\n(resident-clay-angelfish), linked `discovered_from` this bug. Not required for this\nfault's correctness.\n\n**Replication** — pending: re-run of the S3 T3 close on the fixed verifier once change\n2219 lands (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 → Submit)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787673333577284001,"uuid":"da754f58-b565-4548-90d0-68ef25db7c93"}